---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { Aside } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import BrickBoard from '../components/BrickBoard.astro';
import ledger from '../data/ledger.public.json';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url.ts';
import { formatDay } from '../lib/plan.ts';
import { stateLabel, type PublicLedger } from '../lib/ledger.ts';

const led = ledger as unknown as PublicLedger;
const t = led.tests;
const fmt = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US');
const interpreters = led.determinism.interpreters;
const seeds = led.determinism.hash_seeds;
const substrate = led.program.substrate;
const maps = led.program.cognitive_map;
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Substrate status',
    description: "The substrate, Psyche's stage 1 and its foundation: what is built, what is verified, and what was stopped.",
  }}
>
  <Aside type="note" title={`${stateLabel(substrate.state)} and maintained`}>
    The substrate is Psyche's stage 1 and its foundation. Its development has been {substrate.state} since
    {formatDay(substrate.since)} (decision {substrate.decision}), while stage 2, spiking cognitive maps, is
    {maps.state}. No new work starts on the substrate; its tests and checks stay maintained.
  </Aside>

  <p>
    The substrate is a dependency-free Python memory-and-activation substrate. What it shows is that its lower
    layers are correct and deterministic. It makes no claim that any layer reproduces a cognitive effect: three
    attempts to grade one were stopped before any graded run, each at a structurally distinct wall: semantic
    priming was circular, the fan effect found the mechanism absent, and interoception found the signal flat.
    The finding is scoped to this substrate and these three yardsticks. The recurring obstacle, the external
    yardstick, is the lesson stage 2 is built around: classic behavioural tests with published protocols, and
    baselines reproduced against their published behaviour.
  </p>
  <p>
    The captured test run has {t.suites} suites, {fmt.format(t.assertions)} assertions and {t.failures} failures,
    with identical counts on CPython {interpreters.join(', ')} and determinism probed under {seeds.length} hash seeds.
    The meaning bar is {String(led.meaning_bar.status).toLowerCase()}.
  </p>

  <section class="sx-section">
    <h2>Bricks</h2>
    <BrickBoard />
  </section>

  <p>
    Read more: <a href={withBase('substrate/overview/')}>The substrate</a>,
    <a href={withBase('substrate/architecture/')}>Architecture</a> and
    <a href={withBase('substrate/methodology/')}>Methodology</a>.
  </p>
</StarlightPage>
